# ── What was implemented ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- `apps/api/migrations/20260801210000_f45_deletion_cascade.sql`: `artifacts.deleted_at` (+
  `wsx_visible_artifacts()` re-declared with that one predicate added -- the SAME function
  F31/F32/F34 already join through, so browser listing AND download-URL resolution both lose
  a deleted artifact through the ONE doorway); `legal_holds` (read-side for
  `LEGAL_HOLD_ACTIVE`; write side is F46's `applyLegalHold`/`releaseLegalHold`);
  `deletion_tasks` + `deletion_cascade_results` (the six-category outcomes, N-17 encoded as a
  CHECK: `status = 'done' <=> receipt_id IS NOT NULL`); `context_pack_invalidations` (a
  COMPANION table, not a column on `context_packs` -- that table's 0016 pin trigger refuses
  ANY UPDATE on a pinned run, discovered by running the first draft of this migration
  against a pinned fixture row); `provenance_events_type_check` +1 member
  (`deletion-requested`, ADR-101 precedent, Proposed/pending human ratification -- see the
  2026-08-01 addendum in `docs/adr/ADR-101-provenance-event-type-missing-members.md`).
- `apps/api/src/domain/files/deletion-cascade.ts`: pure six-category status derivation
  (`deriveLogicalCascadeStatus`, never returns `"done"` -- that is F46's physical-delete
  worker's transition) and the two-tier SLA deadline math, reusing
  `@repo/contracts/org-admin`'s `WITHDRAWAL_SLA_MS` (the SAME constant F14's
  `withdraw-participant-phone.ts` already uses for the identical D-15 numbers) rather than
  writing `5 * 60_000` / `30 * 86_400_000` a second time.
- `apps/api/src/application/files/deletion-ports.ts`, `preview-delete-impact.ts`,
  `request-deletion.ts`: the two use cases. Cascade ⑤ (`ontology-edges`, the F47 outbound
  port) is attempted OUTSIDE the local transaction that runs cascades ①②③④⑥, so its
  guaranteed phase-01 failure cannot roll back the four/five that succeed -- see
  `request-deletion.ts`'s file header for the full reasoning.
- `apps/api/src/infrastructure/files/pg-deletion-repository.ts`: the four repository
  implementations (`PgDeleteImpactRepository`, `PgLegalHoldGate`,
  `PgCascadeInvalidationRepository`, `PgDeletionTaskRepository`).
- `apps/api/src/domain/identity/project-role-matrix.ts`: new `artifact.requestDeletion`
  action, granted to `facilitator` only (a judgment call -- usecases.md says "项目负责人",
  the four-value role enum has no member by that name; documented at the call site,
  `groupLead`/引导师's ability is left unr36granted as the conservative default, matching the
  UI's own conservative default for "delete individual version" -- both are [待定], not
  decided here).
- `packages/contracts/src/provenance.ts` + `docs/adr/ADR-101-...md`: +1
  `ProvenanceEventType` member, following the established ADR-101 precedent exactly (F32/
  F117/F109/F34/F98/F112 all did this the same way).
- `apps/web/lib/mock/interview-studio.ts` / `apps/web/lib/mock/rec.ts`: two pre-existing
  `lint-withdrawal-flow.mjs` false positives fixed by reformatting (splitting unrelated
  sentences that happened to share one physical line) -- no semantic change, both predate
  this branch and were blocking the required web-lint verification command.

# ── Known, documented gaps (not silently omitted) ──────────────────────────────────────

- `previewDeleteImpact.referencingReportSections` is always `[]` -- phase-01 has no
  report-section table (10-report/13-deliv are phase-02), matching
  `files.KNOWN_CONTRACT_GAPS.FS11`'s own framing.
- `exportedOutOfOrg` covers the single-file export path (`download_grants`, purpose=export,
  consumed) only -- the batch zip path (`export_jobs`) records an item COUNT, not which
  artifact ids were in it, so it cannot be joined per-artifact without a schema change F45
  did not need to make. Documented at `PgDeleteImpactRepository.countsFor`'s call site.
- Cascade ⑤ (`ontology-edges`) is ALWAYS `"failed"` in phase-01 -- `invalidateOntologyEdges`
  is F47's contract stub, guaranteed to throw. This makes `requestDeletion` ALWAYS produce
  `"partial-failure"` today, by design (N-17: no receipt while any category is unresolved).
  The counter-proof test in `delete-six-cascade-invalidation.test.ts` substitutes a fake
  "09-kg arrived" implementation to prove the orchestration itself reaches `"running"`/all-ok
  once that dependency exists -- this is `KNOWN_CONTRACT_GAPS.FS11` made observable, not a
  bug to silently work around.
- `agentRunId`/agent-actor detection for `AGENT_CANNOT_DELETE` is an explicit `actorKind`
  input parameter rather than inferred from the caller's identity, matching the existing
  `creator_kind`/`agentRunId` explicit-input convention (`artifact_versions`, F44). Wiring
  this to a real caller-identity signal is an interface-layer concern outside this feature's
  scope (no HTTP controller was added -- see below).
- No HTTP controller was added for `previewDeleteImpact`/`requestDeletion` in this pass. Every
  other `uc-22-4` operation this feature depends on or hands off to (F46's
  `getDeletionTask`/`listTrashQueue`/`retryCascade`/`applyLegalHold`/`getDeletionReceipt`)
  is also controller-less today; F44 (version list/derived model) shipped the same way
  (application-layer only, tested directly). Wiring the HTTP surface is left to whichever
  feature wires the `files` bundle's routes end to end -- flagged here rather than silently
  assumed done.
